# M7: the build context is now the repo root (see Dockerfile's own
# comments) since the image builds both services/frontend/ and
# services/backend-api/. Without this file, Docker would upload the whole
# working tree (including .git/) to the daemon on every build, and a
# locally-installed services/frontend/node_modules/ would get copied
# straight into the image by `COPY services/frontend/ ./` -- silently
# overwriting the clean `npm ci` output the frontend-build stage just
# produced, with whatever happens to be on the host's filesystem.
.git/
**/node_modules
services/frontend/dist
services/backend-api/__pycache__/
services/backend-api/*.pyc
services/backend-api/.pytest_cache/
services/backend-api/registry.db
# Same class of leak, different direction: services/backend-api/static/
# is a local placeholder (or a stale local `npm run build` output) that
# main.py's own tests need on disk -- see its own .gitignore entry. The
# Dockerfile's `COPY services/backend-api/ .` runs BEFORE the frontend
# stage's `COPY --from=frontend-build /frontend/dist ./static`, and
# Docker's COPY into an existing directory merges rather than replaces --
# so without this exclusion, any stale local file here would ride along
# into the image underneath the real build output.
services/backend-api/static
